The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (req->flags & DRM_V3D_PERFMON_CLEAR_GLOBAL) {
        if (!v3d->global_perfmon)
                return -EINVAL;
        xchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, NULL);
        return 0;
}
```
```c
if (cmpxchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, NULL, perfmon))
        return -EBUSY;
```
```c
cmpxchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, perfmon, NULL);
```
Reason:
`v3d_perfmon_find()` increments the reference count of the perfmon. In the CLEAR_GLOBAL path, both the reference from `v3d_perfmon_find()` (via `perfmon`) and the reference previously stored in `v3d->global_perfmon` are leaked because no `v3d_perfmon_put()` is called. In the `EBUSY` path, the reference from `v3d_perfmon_find()` is leaked on an early return. In `v3d_perfmon_delete()`, when destroying the global perfmon, the reference stashed by `SET_GLOBAL` is not released after setting the pointer to `NULL`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
v3d_perfmon_put(perfmon);
old = xchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, NULL);
if (!old)
        return -EINVAL;
v3d_perfmon_put(old);
```
```c
if (cmpxchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, NULL, perfmon)) {
        v3d_perfmon_put(perfmon);
        return -EBUSY;
}
```
```c
if (cmpxchg(&v3d->global_perfmon, perfmon, NULL) == perfmon)
        v3d_perfmon_put(perfmon);
```
Reason:
The fix explicitly releases the reference from `v3d_perfmon_find()` on the CLEAR_GLOBAL path before handling the old global perfmon, and also releases the old global perfmon reference. On the `EBUSY` path, the find reference is released before returning. In `v3d_perfmon_delete()`, before putting the perfmon itself, the reference stored from `SET_GLOBAL` is released only if it was the current global perfmon. This ensures all acquired references are properly balanced.

